1
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:23,073
They are an army unlike any other.

2
00:01:23,282 --> 00:01:27,119
Crusading across the stars
toward a place called UnderVerse,

3
00:01:27,244 --> 00:01:31,415
their promised land.
A constellation of dark new worlds.

4
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:34,710
Necromongers they're called.

5
00:01:35,085 --> 00:01:38,923
And if they cannot convert you,
they will kill you.

6
00:01:40,549 --> 00:01:43,260
Leading them, the Lord Marshal.

7
00:01:44,595 --> 00:01:48,265
He alone has made a pilgrimage
to the gates of the UnderVerse

8
00:01:48,349 --> 00:01:50,643
and returned a different being.

9
00:01:52,144 --> 00:01:56,815
Stronger. Stranger.
Half alive and half

10
00:01:58,359 --> 00:01:59,944
something else.

11
00:02:11,622 --> 00:02:15,167
If we are to survive,
a new balance must be found.

12
00:02:16,293 --> 00:02:19,463
In normal times,
evil would be fought by good.

13
00:02:19,547 --> 00:02:21,340
But in times like these,

14
00:02:21,423 --> 00:02:25,261
well, it should be fought
by another kind of evil.

15
00:02:59,962 --> 00:03:01,422
Lining him up for you.

16
00:03:01,505 --> 00:03:03,257
Portside shot coming up.

17
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:05,009
Steady. Here we go.

18
00:03:12,308 --> 00:03:13,475
Steady.

19
00:03:15,269 --> 00:03:19,273
Take it! Take a shot!

20
00:03:21,692 --> 00:03:22,776
Shit.

21
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:26,280
- Toombs, we're running out of rope!
- Shut up! I got it! Again!

22
00:03:29,408 --> 00:03:30,492
Now!

23
00:03:33,871 --> 00:03:35,039
Toombs!

24
00:03:48,927 --> 00:03:50,262
Riddick.

25
00:03:54,041 --> 00:03:56,226
I don't know, Toombs.
Looks kind of tight.

26
00:03:56,310 --> 00:03:59,897
Not where I'm sitting.
This is the biggest payday ever.

27
00:04:00,230 --> 00:04:03,484
So throw on a fresh pair of panties.
Let's get this right.

28
00:04:13,535 --> 00:04:17,081
Three meters clearance portside.
One and a half meters starboard.

29
00:04:18,207 --> 00:04:20,125
We got a choke point coming up.

30
00:04:32,971 --> 00:04:34,890
What the Shit was that?

31
00:04:37,017 --> 00:04:39,186
Tags, you got eyes on Riddick?

32
00:04:40,646 --> 00:04:41,814
Tags?

33
00:04:46,944 --> 00:04:48,195
Jesus.

34
00:04:49,697 --> 00:04:52,950
He just ghosted two guys,
and I never even saw him.

35
00:04:54,451 --> 00:04:56,453
What do you think?
Maybe we ought to just...

36
00:04:56,537 --> 00:04:59,456
I think you're my new gunner.
Grab a Gat.

37
00:05:08,090 --> 00:05:10,300
Stay on top of him this time.

38
00:05:37,745 --> 00:05:39,747
You made three mistakes.

39
00:05:42,833 --> 00:05:45,669
First, you took the job.

40
00:05:46,336 --> 00:05:48,797
Second, you came light.

41
00:05:49,131 --> 00:05:52,926
A four-man crew for me?
Fucking insulting.

42
00:05:53,177 --> 00:05:55,637
But the worst mistake you made...

43
00:05:58,974 --> 00:06:00,517
Empty gun rack.

44
00:06:04,688 --> 00:06:08,108
- What's the bounty on my head?
- 1 mil.

45
00:06:10,944 --> 00:06:12,196
1.5.

46
00:06:12,321 --> 00:06:15,365
What slam pays 1.5 for a convict?

47
00:06:15,866 --> 00:06:17,284
Private party.

48
00:06:18,827 --> 00:06:22,498
Guy! Easy! Anonymous.
That's what the sheet said.

49
00:06:22,873 --> 00:06:24,333
What planet?

50
00:06:26,001 --> 00:06:27,503
Helion Prime.

51
00:06:35,051 --> 00:06:38,222
Where you going?
Last question.

52
00:06:38,472 --> 00:06:41,225
And you better get this one
right, mere.

53
00:06:42,142 --> 00:06:43,894
Whose ship is this?

54
00:06:45,103 --> 00:06:46,313
Mine?

55
00:07:06,542 --> 00:07:11,421
Knew they'd come for me.
Took them five years, but I knew.

56
00:07:12,256 --> 00:07:16,885
You don't expect these mercs
to have any honor, any code.

57
00:07:18,595 --> 00:07:21,765
But this new bounty
from a holy man,

58
00:07:23,058 --> 00:07:25,227
a guy whose neck I saved.

59
00:07:27,396 --> 00:07:31,441
Well, lesson learned.
No such word as "friend."

60
00:07:32,276 --> 00:07:35,696
Can only end bad
when you let someone get too close.

61
00:07:37,906 --> 00:07:39,366
Bad for them.

62
00:07:41,451 --> 00:07:45,706
So now it's back to all the
brightness, and everything I hate.

63
00:07:48,041 --> 00:07:50,419
I wonder if she'll be there.

64
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:03,015
Act like an animal
and I'm gonna slot you up like one.

65
00:08:03,098 --> 00:08:05,017
This one is always in trouble.

66
00:08:05,601 --> 00:08:07,352
I knew it. I smell it.

67
00:08:28,707 --> 00:08:30,208
Get in there!

68
00:08:55,817 --> 00:08:58,445
Can we shut the goddamn noise?

69
00:09:30,394 --> 00:09:33,981
They say most of your brain
shuts down in cryosleep.

70
00:09:34,064 --> 00:09:36,274
Brain shuts down in cryosleep.

71
00:09:37,943 --> 00:09:40,988
All but the primitive side.

72
00:09:41,071 --> 00:09:42,656
The animal side.

73
00:09:43,615 --> 00:09:46,410
All but the Furyan side.

74
00:09:51,915 --> 00:09:54,084
Some of us still remember
the true crime

75
00:09:54,167 --> 00:09:56,211
that happened here on Furya.

76
00:09:59,297 --> 00:10:01,216
And once you wake,

77
00:10:02,175 --> 00:10:04,302
truly wake,

78
00:10:07,305 --> 00:10:09,224
you'll remember, too.

79
00:10:15,188 --> 00:10:17,941
Helion Prime is on alert condition four.

80
00:10:18,025 --> 00:10:20,777
All unrecognized craft
will be escorted to the ground

81
00:10:20,861 --> 00:10:22,529
for security inspections.

82
00:10:22,612 --> 00:10:24,865
Unrecognized craft,
you need to follow me

83
00:10:24,948 --> 00:10:27,325
to Spaceport 6
for security inspections.

84
00:10:29,953 --> 00:10:33,790
Do you hear me?
Follow me to Spaceport 6 now!

85
00:11:23,924 --> 00:11:26,051
Imam, pray for us.

86
00:11:26,134 --> 00:11:28,970
It was confirmed
two seasons back. Yes.

87
00:11:30,097 --> 00:11:31,973
They're coming here.
I mean, are we next?

88
00:11:32,057 --> 00:11:33,266
Militants storm...

89
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:36,394
Yes, we're going to
the underground shelters if it happens...

90
00:11:36,478 --> 00:11:38,522
That's what I heard, too.

91
00:11:39,106 --> 00:11:41,024
Are you staying or leaving?

92
00:11:42,025 --> 00:11:44,361
It's the end of everything.
Everything!

93
00:11:44,778 --> 00:11:47,531
- My neighbors...
- Half my street is gone.

94
00:11:47,864 --> 00:11:50,325
- What are we gonna do?
- I don't know.

95
00:11:50,408 --> 00:11:52,786
Hood of the devil.
That's what someone called them.

96
00:11:52,869 --> 00:11:54,955
- Who is them?
- Some kind of new creature...

97
00:11:55,038 --> 00:11:57,457
It's all nonsense.
Everyone is over-reacting.

98
00:11:57,541 --> 00:12:00,127
...so tall
that it touches the clouds.

99
00:12:00,377 --> 00:12:03,713
And there's nothing around
this statue, this colossus.

100
00:12:03,797 --> 00:12:06,800
Nothing left.
It's their calling card.

101
00:12:16,977 --> 00:12:19,688
Did you know
all your doors were locked?

102
00:12:26,236 --> 00:12:30,073
Five years ago,
I took two people off that planet.

103
00:12:30,574 --> 00:12:34,911
A kid, Jack, who everyone else
thought was a boy

104
00:12:35,829 --> 00:12:40,417
and a holy man
searching for New Mecca.

105
00:12:44,796 --> 00:12:46,131
Your wife.

106
00:12:48,133 --> 00:12:49,759
She's in the shower.

107
00:12:51,261 --> 00:12:55,932
I told one man where I might go.

108
00:12:58,018 --> 00:13:01,563
I showed trust to one man.

109
00:13:03,273 --> 00:13:05,025
Did I make a mistake, Imam?

110
00:13:06,276 --> 00:13:08,111
There is no simple answer...

111
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:12,240
Whatever was said
was meant to give us a chance.

112
00:13:12,782 --> 00:13:14,492
A fighting chance.

113
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:17,162
Were it not
for the threat of invasion

114
00:13:17,245 --> 00:13:20,123
I never would have betrayed you.
I give you my word, Riddick.

115
00:13:20,207 --> 00:13:21,458
Riddick!

116
00:13:25,128 --> 00:13:26,129
Riddick!

117
00:13:28,882 --> 00:13:30,550
And a daughter...

118
00:13:33,011 --> 00:13:35,972
- No.
- ...whose name would be...

119
00:13:36,056 --> 00:13:38,642
If you have issue with me,
you let it be with me.

120
00:13:38,725 --> 00:13:40,644
You need not know their names.

121
00:13:40,810 --> 00:13:44,731
Ziza. My name is Ziza.

122
00:13:47,025 --> 00:13:48,026
Ziza.

123
00:13:50,779 --> 00:13:51,905
Cute kid.

124
00:13:51,988 --> 00:13:54,199
Did you really kill monsters?

125
00:13:54,366 --> 00:13:57,077
The ones that were gonna hurt
my father?

126
00:13:58,662 --> 00:14:00,914
Such are our bedtime stories.

127
00:14:01,206 --> 00:14:03,333
Go, Ziza. Go on.

128
00:14:08,296 --> 00:14:12,050
So now who do I have to kill
to get this payday off my head?

129
00:14:28,525 --> 00:14:32,237
It is said the comet
always precedes them.

130
00:14:33,071 --> 00:14:34,823
These world-Enders.

131
00:14:38,368 --> 00:14:42,455
The Coalsack planets are gone.
Eight million settlers missing.

132
00:14:42,914 --> 00:14:45,583
The entire Aquilan System
is gone, too.

133
00:14:46,501 --> 00:14:50,046
Helion Prime shares its sunlight
with all worlds nearby.

134
00:14:52,590 --> 00:14:55,885
If we fall, they fall.

135
00:14:57,304 --> 00:14:58,888
And after that...

136
00:15:00,890 --> 00:15:02,976
My God, how do I save my family?

137
00:15:08,815 --> 00:15:11,067
Have you heard anything I've said?

138
00:15:13,028 --> 00:15:16,156
You said it's all circling
the drain. The whole universe.

139
00:15:16,698 --> 00:15:18,491
- Right?
- That's right.

140
00:15:27,417 --> 00:15:29,169
Had to end sometime.

141
00:15:46,853 --> 00:15:49,064
The one you want is now here.

142
00:16:07,207 --> 00:16:09,209
And whose throat is this?

143
00:16:10,418 --> 00:16:12,128
If you cut my throat,

144
00:16:12,212 --> 00:16:15,590
I'll not be able to rescind
the offer that brought you here.

145
00:16:15,673 --> 00:16:17,967
Nor tell you
why it's so vital that you did come.

146
00:16:18,051 --> 00:16:20,345
The blade comes off
when the bounty comes off.

147
00:16:20,428 --> 00:16:23,890
This is Aereon.
An envoy from the Elemental race.

148
00:16:24,808 --> 00:16:26,726
She means you no harm.

149
00:16:30,897 --> 00:16:32,065
There are very few of us

150
00:16:32,148 --> 00:16:35,026
who have met a Necromonger
and lived to speak of it.

151
00:16:35,110 --> 00:16:39,322
So when I choose to speak of it,
you should choose to listen.

152
00:16:39,781 --> 00:16:41,116
Necromonger.

153
00:16:41,199 --> 00:16:45,078
It is the name that will convert or kill

154
00:16:45,161 --> 00:16:46,955
every last human life.

155
00:16:47,330 --> 00:16:49,874
Unless the universe
can rebalance itself.

156
00:16:51,376 --> 00:16:53,670
Maybe you should pretend
like you're talking to

157
00:16:53,753 --> 00:16:56,089
someone educated
in the penal system.

158
00:16:56,172 --> 00:16:58,883
In fact, don't pretend.

159
00:16:59,592 --> 00:17:02,345
Balance is everything to Elementals.

160
00:17:02,637 --> 00:17:04,848
Water to fire. Earth to air.

161
00:17:05,306 --> 00:17:07,434
We have 33 different words for it.

162
00:17:07,642 --> 00:17:09,185
But now we have only time

163
00:17:09,269 --> 00:17:11,438
to speak of
the balance of opposites.

164
00:17:11,521 --> 00:17:14,899
There is a story, Riddick,
of young male Furyans

165
00:17:15,525 --> 00:17:19,654
strangled at birth.
Strangled with their own cords.

166
00:17:22,031 --> 00:17:25,326
When Aereon told this story
to the Helion leaders,

167
00:17:25,410 --> 00:17:26,870
I told her of you.

168
00:17:26,953 --> 00:17:28,538
What do you know
of your early years?

169
00:17:28,621 --> 00:17:31,499
Do you remember your homeworld?
Where it was?

170
00:17:31,583 --> 00:17:34,711
- Have you met any others?
- Others like yourself.

171
00:17:37,589 --> 00:17:40,717
Sister, they don't know
what to do with just one of me.

172
00:17:41,468 --> 00:17:45,388
- Open up in there! Open up!
- Stand back!

173
00:17:46,806 --> 00:17:48,600
They are searching houses.

174
00:17:48,683 --> 00:17:50,435
They look for a man
who came here today.

175
00:17:50,518 --> 00:17:52,395
- They think he might be a spy.
- A spy.

176
00:17:52,479 --> 00:17:55,023
Did someone see him come here today?
Did they?

177
00:17:55,106 --> 00:17:56,566
Lajjun, stop!

178
00:17:57,150 --> 00:18:00,904
I will send them away.
But wait one minute, please.

179
00:18:01,237 --> 00:18:04,199
Will you wait one minute
to save worlds?

180
00:18:05,658 --> 00:18:07,160
Not my fight.

181
00:18:07,869 --> 00:18:10,747
So you will leave us to our fate?

182
00:18:11,915 --> 00:18:14,417
- Just like you did her.
- Break it down!

183
00:18:18,588 --> 00:18:19,631
Get in!

184
00:18:19,714 --> 00:18:22,175
Come, let us try to send them away.

185
00:18:24,677 --> 00:18:26,346
- Just let me have her!
- Come on.

186
00:18:26,429 --> 00:18:27,680
Leave us alone.

187
00:18:29,724 --> 00:18:31,392
There is no one here.

188
00:18:32,185 --> 00:18:34,896
You don't understand.
He can help us!

189
00:18:34,979 --> 00:18:36,648
He can help us!

190
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:50,286
You're not afraid of the dark,
are you?

191
00:19:10,598 --> 00:19:12,475
- Get him!
- Where is he?

192
00:19:13,601 --> 00:19:14,769
In here.

193
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,591
You mentioned her.

194
00:19:48,678 --> 00:19:50,638
She went looking for you.

195
00:19:50,722 --> 00:19:53,891
People died. She went to prison.

196
00:19:54,642 --> 00:19:57,145
I don't remember where.

197
00:19:58,187 --> 00:20:03,109
But it was a world so hot, you
couldn't survive on the surface.

198
00:20:03,818 --> 00:20:05,194
Crematoria.

199
00:20:05,570 --> 00:20:09,240
Young Jack. She thought of you
as her older brother.

200
00:20:09,699 --> 00:20:13,077
- She worshipped you.
- You were supposed to watch her.

201
00:20:13,870 --> 00:20:17,582
She never forgave you for leaving

202
00:20:18,499 --> 00:20:22,754
- just when she needed you most.
- She needed to stay away from me.

203
00:20:24,213 --> 00:20:25,590
You all do.

204
00:20:27,550 --> 00:20:28,551
Riddick!

205
00:20:32,472 --> 00:20:35,141
Are you gonna stop
the new monsters now?

206
00:20:47,904 --> 00:20:51,074
Furyans. Defiant to the end.

207
00:21:29,570 --> 00:21:32,615
No, no. We go to the shelter.

208
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:35,952
We take only ourselves.

209
00:21:51,134 --> 00:21:53,428
Turn back!
Go to the other shelter.

210
00:21:53,511 --> 00:21:54,595
There is no room.

211
00:21:54,679 --> 00:21:57,056
- They won't let us in!
- Get back.

212
00:21:58,307 --> 00:21:59,559
Stay close.

213
00:23:46,165 --> 00:23:48,793
Flight leaders,
get all squads off the ground now.

214
00:23:48,876 --> 00:23:50,586
We have heavy inbound.

215
00:23:52,797 --> 00:23:54,257
Follow me in!

216
00:24:02,056 --> 00:24:03,850
They're coming back!

217
00:24:13,150 --> 00:24:14,986
The next shelter. This way!

218
00:24:41,929 --> 00:24:43,806
I'll see if it's safe.

219
00:24:49,103 --> 00:24:51,314
- Stay back.
- Come, Ziza.

220
00:25:11,751 --> 00:25:12,835
Come!

221
00:25:32,855 --> 00:25:34,607
You following me?

222
00:26:11,894 --> 00:26:13,562
Lajjun and Ziza!

223
00:26:14,063 --> 00:26:15,189
When it's over.

224
00:26:15,272 --> 00:26:18,234
- Let me go. I must get to my family.
- When it's over.

225
00:26:46,387 --> 00:26:48,180
I borrowed a ship.

226
00:26:48,556 --> 00:26:51,726
You can ride along if you
don't mind riding with a convict.

227
00:26:51,809 --> 00:26:54,812
I thank you, but I must get
my family across the river.

228
00:26:54,895 --> 00:26:57,440
God willing, there is still
a shelter I can get them...

229
00:26:57,523 --> 00:26:59,650
I'm sure God has his tricks.

230
00:27:00,109 --> 00:27:02,695
But getting out of places
no one else can,

231
00:27:02,778 --> 00:27:04,613
that's one of mine.

232
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:08,075
Let's get your family.

233
00:27:42,735 --> 00:27:43,944
In here.

234
00:27:45,529 --> 00:27:46,781
Get in.

235
00:28:56,517 --> 00:28:58,727
- Imam.
- Don't follow me.

236
00:30:33,489 --> 00:30:35,908
There will be an afterlife for me.

237
00:30:38,410 --> 00:30:40,329
Will there be for you?

238
00:31:58,407 --> 00:32:00,576
Let's go replenish the ranks.

239
00:32:14,131 --> 00:32:18,802
Never fails to inspire, does it?
Each time a dynasty falls.

240
00:32:18,927 --> 00:32:22,097
Remember your place, Dame Vaako.

241
00:32:22,681 --> 00:32:25,517
My place is at your side,
dear husband.

242
00:32:25,809 --> 00:32:28,103
From here till UnderVerse come.

243
00:32:52,961 --> 00:32:54,671
In this 'verse

244
00:32:55,756 --> 00:32:59,593
life is antagonistic
to the natural state.

245
00:33:01,011 --> 00:33:05,307
Here, humans
in all their various races

246
00:33:06,475 --> 00:33:08,519
are a spontaneous outbreak,

247
00:33:09,645 --> 00:33:11,563
an unguided mistake.

248
00:33:12,398 --> 00:33:16,902
Our purpose is to correct
that mistake.

249
00:33:19,029 --> 00:33:21,323
Because there is another 'verse.

250
00:33:22,324 --> 00:33:26,662
A 'verse where life
is welcomed and cherished.

251
00:33:27,496 --> 00:33:30,499
A ravishing, ever-new place

252
00:33:30,666 --> 00:33:32,334
called UnderVerse.

253
00:33:34,420 --> 00:33:37,047
But the road to that 'verse

254
00:33:38,424 --> 00:33:40,426
crosses over the threshold.

255
00:33:40,509 --> 00:33:43,846
Threshold!
Take us to the threshold!

256
00:33:44,263 --> 00:33:46,890
What you call death.

257
00:33:49,518 --> 00:33:53,230
So it is this 'verse
that must be cleansed of life

258
00:33:53,397 --> 00:33:56,942
so that UnderVerse
can populate and prosper.

259
00:34:00,195 --> 00:34:04,158
Look around you.
Every Necromonger in this hall,

260
00:34:04,700 --> 00:34:06,452
every one of the Legion Vast

261
00:34:06,535 --> 00:34:09,788
that just swept aside your defenses
in one night

262
00:34:09,997 --> 00:34:11,623
was once like you.

263
00:34:12,207 --> 00:34:14,710
Fought as feebly as you.

264
00:34:16,170 --> 00:34:21,049
Every Necromonger
that lives today is a convert.

265
00:34:21,133 --> 00:34:22,843
There'll be no conversions!

266
00:34:22,926 --> 00:34:25,888
We all began as something else!

267
00:34:28,515 --> 00:34:32,436
It was hard for me to accept, too,
when I first heard these words.

268
00:34:33,103 --> 00:34:34,563
But I changed.

269
00:34:35,772 --> 00:34:38,400
I let them take away my pain.

270
00:34:38,484 --> 00:34:39,818
You betrayed your faith.

271
00:34:39,902 --> 00:34:42,571
Just as you will change

272
00:34:42,738 --> 00:34:47,576
when you realize that the threshold
to the UnderVerse will be crossed

273
00:34:47,910 --> 00:34:51,955
only by those who have embraced
the Necromonger faith.

274
00:34:52,164 --> 00:34:55,167
For those of you who will
right now

275
00:34:55,292 --> 00:34:59,505
drop to your knees
and ask to be purified.

276
00:34:59,588 --> 00:35:03,884
- We will not renounce our faith!
- No one here will do what you ask.

277
00:35:04,426 --> 00:35:06,053
It is unthinkable!

278
00:35:06,303 --> 00:35:10,140
This is a world of many peoples,
many religions!

279
00:35:10,933 --> 00:35:15,270
And we simply cannot
and will not be converted.

280
00:35:16,355 --> 00:35:18,357
Then I'll take your soul.

281
00:35:29,993 --> 00:35:31,370
Join him

282
00:35:33,789 --> 00:35:35,165
or join me.

283
00:35:55,852 --> 00:35:57,813
This is your one chance.

284
00:35:58,480 --> 00:36:01,400
Take the Lord Marshal's offer
and bow.

285
00:36:02,442 --> 00:36:04,027
I bow to no man.

286
00:36:11,076 --> 00:36:12,619
He's not a man.

287
00:36:13,120 --> 00:36:16,456
He's the holy Half-Dead
who has seen the UnderVerse.

288
00:36:16,832 --> 00:36:19,209
Look, I'm not with everyone here.

289
00:36:20,377 --> 00:36:22,671
But I will take a piece of him.

290
00:36:29,261 --> 00:36:31,138
A piece you will have.

291
00:36:59,249 --> 00:37:00,584
Stop him!

292
00:37:13,180 --> 00:37:16,016
Irgun. One of my best.

293
00:37:16,850 --> 00:37:18,352
If you say so.

294
00:37:22,272 --> 00:37:24,608
What do you think of this blade?

295
00:37:33,784 --> 00:37:36,703
I think it's a half-gram heavy
on the back end.

296
00:37:36,828 --> 00:37:40,165
In our faith,
you keep what you kill.

297
00:37:47,589 --> 00:37:49,758
Are you familiar to me?

298
00:37:52,177 --> 00:37:55,514
Have we met on some distant field?

299
00:37:57,599 --> 00:37:59,309
You'd think I'd remember.

300
00:38:00,477 --> 00:38:02,646
You'd think I would, too.

301
00:38:04,606 --> 00:38:06,692
Take him before the Quasi-Deads.

302
00:38:14,241 --> 00:38:16,660
Perhaps the breeder would do it

303
00:38:17,869 --> 00:38:19,955
if somebody just asked him.

304
00:38:23,041 --> 00:38:24,793
It is a rare offer.

305
00:38:26,628 --> 00:38:29,589
A visit inside Necropolis.

306
00:38:31,717 --> 00:38:35,220
It's been a long time
since I smelled beautiful.

307
00:38:36,513 --> 00:38:38,515
Let me show you the way.

308
00:39:32,319 --> 00:39:35,614
Beautiful eyes. Come.

309
00:39:39,284 --> 00:39:42,412
The last six Lord Marshals
have called this home.

310
00:39:43,413 --> 00:39:45,290
Magnificent, isn't it?

311
00:39:46,249 --> 00:39:49,836
- I might have gone a different way.
- True of us all.

312
00:39:52,464 --> 00:39:55,509
Converts receiving the mark
of the Necromonger.

313
00:39:58,970 --> 00:40:01,640
They learn how one pain
can lessen another.

314
00:40:15,737 --> 00:40:17,072
There now.

315
00:40:18,782 --> 00:40:22,786
That is just perfect.

316
00:40:26,998 --> 00:40:29,125
The more you resist them

317
00:40:29,501 --> 00:40:31,837
the greater the damage will be.

318
00:40:34,589 --> 00:40:36,049
A new one.

319
00:40:36,132 --> 00:40:39,719
You've brought us a new one.

320
00:40:54,901 --> 00:40:56,653
Interesting breeder.

321
00:41:12,460 --> 00:41:13,962
Making entry.

322
00:41:15,171 --> 00:41:17,132
This won't take long.

323
00:41:18,466 --> 00:41:21,553
We've entered his neocortex.

324
00:41:23,013 --> 00:41:25,307
- The Riddick!
- Regress.

325
00:41:26,641 --> 00:41:28,810
Scanning fresh memories.

326
00:41:28,894 --> 00:41:32,230
Thoughts of someone called Jack.

327
00:41:33,023 --> 00:41:34,149
Riddick!

328
00:41:36,860 --> 00:41:38,862
She went to prison.

329
00:41:39,946 --> 00:41:43,033
Now we find thoughts
of an Elemental.

330
00:41:43,491 --> 00:41:46,244
The one race that would slow
the spread of Necromongers.

331
00:41:46,328 --> 00:41:47,329
Furyans.

332
00:41:47,412 --> 00:41:49,664
Furyans.

333
00:41:53,793 --> 00:41:55,754
Where does he come from?

334
00:41:55,837 --> 00:42:00,050
Who are his people?
These are the things I need to know.

335
00:42:03,511 --> 00:42:05,096
We find energy.

336
00:42:07,349 --> 00:42:10,101
You must settle your past.

337
00:42:11,394 --> 00:42:13,688
We find Furyan energy.

338
00:42:14,731 --> 00:42:15,941
For all of us.

339
00:42:16,024 --> 00:42:17,651
He's Furyan!

340
00:42:18,568 --> 00:42:20,028
Furyan!

341
00:42:22,238 --> 00:42:24,032
A Furyan survivor!

342
00:42:26,034 --> 00:42:27,744
Look at our world,

343
00:42:28,078 --> 00:42:31,373
at the graves of those who didn't
escape 30 years ago.

344
00:42:31,498 --> 00:42:34,542
There is no future
until we settle our past.

345
00:42:37,212 --> 00:42:39,881
For all of us who bear the mark.

346
00:42:40,966 --> 00:42:42,550
Kill the Furyan!

347
00:42:42,634 --> 00:42:44,761
Kill the Riddick!

348
00:42:48,223 --> 00:42:49,683
Kill the Riddick.

349
00:43:23,425 --> 00:43:25,135
Who is this man?

350
00:43:27,095 --> 00:43:30,015
Find him. Whatever it takes.
Find him.

351
00:44:05,175 --> 00:44:08,636
Let me guess.
A five-man crew this time.

352
00:44:09,596 --> 00:44:12,515
Couple of things
you could have done better.

353
00:44:16,519 --> 00:44:21,191
First, trash the locater beacon
inside my ship, the one you jacked.

354
00:44:21,524 --> 00:44:24,778
And second, and this is really
the more important part,

355
00:44:25,195 --> 00:44:28,156
dust my dick
when you get the chance.

356
00:44:28,907 --> 00:44:31,159
- Any questions?
- Yeah.

357
00:44:34,412 --> 00:44:36,331
What took you so long?

358
00:44:44,214 --> 00:44:45,423
Let's go, big boy.

359
00:44:58,061 --> 00:45:00,855
In and out.
Unsuspected and undetected.

360
00:45:00,939 --> 00:45:03,066
Damn, I love a good smash-and-grab!

361
00:45:03,149 --> 00:45:06,194
Not so fast, dickheads.

362
00:45:06,277 --> 00:45:07,695
We're picking up fields here.

363
00:45:07,779 --> 00:45:10,532
Unknown fields detected on hull.

364
00:45:10,907 --> 00:45:13,993
- I knew it. Here it comes.
- This is some kind of scan.

365
00:45:14,536 --> 00:45:16,746
I don't know.
Reading our BTUs, maybe?

366
00:45:16,830 --> 00:45:19,749
- Let's drop one.
- Dropping.

367
00:45:28,758 --> 00:45:30,218
Decoy launched.

368
00:45:35,431 --> 00:45:37,934
Preparing to engage ion drive.

369
00:45:38,017 --> 00:45:41,938
So where do we drop
your Merc-killing ass?

370
00:45:42,605 --> 00:45:46,234
Who's gonna pay
the most for you now? Butcher Bay?

371
00:45:46,401 --> 00:45:47,861
Butcher Bay?

372
00:45:48,945 --> 00:45:52,240
Ten minutes every other day
on the dog-run.

373
00:45:52,323 --> 00:45:54,576
Protein waffles aren't bad.

374
00:45:55,618 --> 00:45:59,164
How about Ursa Luna?
Nice little double-max prison.

375
00:45:59,247 --> 00:46:03,376
They keep a cell open for me,
just in case I drop in.

376
00:46:03,543 --> 00:46:05,753
You know the problem
with these joints now?

377
00:46:05,837 --> 00:46:08,089
Health clubs
for waffle-eating pussies.

378
00:46:08,173 --> 00:46:11,134
Maybe we should think about
upping our game here a little bit.

379
00:46:11,217 --> 00:46:13,636
Think about some place
truly diabolical.

380
00:46:13,720 --> 00:46:15,513
What the hell is he thinking now?

381
00:46:15,597 --> 00:46:19,726
He's thinking a triple-max prison.
A no-daylight slam.

382
00:46:19,809 --> 00:46:21,644
Only three of them
left in this system,

383
00:46:21,728 --> 00:46:23,062
two of them out of range

384
00:46:23,146 --> 00:46:26,191
for a shitty little under cutter
like this one with no legs.

385
00:46:26,274 --> 00:46:28,860
Leaving just one.

386
00:46:29,944 --> 00:46:31,362
Crematoria.

387
00:46:32,113 --> 00:46:35,241
That is what you had in mind,
right, Toombs?

388
00:46:35,491 --> 00:46:38,286
How does he know
where we're going, and we don't?

389
00:46:38,369 --> 00:46:40,538
- Dope it out.
- I hate this run.

390
00:46:40,622 --> 00:46:42,498
Just do it!

391
00:46:42,582 --> 00:46:45,210
Don't know about
this new crew of yours.

392
00:46:45,293 --> 00:46:47,170
They seem a bit skittish.

393
00:46:47,253 --> 00:46:50,965
Probably shouldn't tell them
what happened to the last crew.

394
00:46:59,182 --> 00:47:02,810
You know, you were supposed to be
some slick-shit killer.

395
00:47:04,020 --> 00:47:08,691
Now look at you.
All back-of-the-bus and shit.

396
00:47:46,521 --> 00:47:50,692
I say we attack Helion Two next.
Take it straight into their teeth.

397
00:47:50,775 --> 00:47:53,653
It'll cost you 20,000 heads,
5 Warrior Ships,

398
00:47:53,736 --> 00:47:57,448
- nothing more, I swear it.
- While I do prize brute force

399
00:47:57,824 --> 00:48:01,286
this approach is,
perhaps, more artful.

400
00:48:01,953 --> 00:48:05,915
Start at the end.
Go straight to Helion Five,

401
00:48:06,040 --> 00:48:08,167
the last planet in the system.

402
00:48:08,251 --> 00:48:10,878
We approach from the night side.

403
00:48:11,004 --> 00:48:13,172
Remove these cannon first,

404
00:48:13,464 --> 00:48:16,301
then attack the larger placements
at speed.

405
00:48:16,467 --> 00:48:18,636
We'll catch them
on their rear flank.

406
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:20,513
And in 10 days' time

407
00:48:20,638 --> 00:48:23,725
the rest of those worlds
will tumble before us.

408
00:48:24,309 --> 00:48:25,727
You see, as with most,

409
00:48:25,810 --> 00:48:29,689
their blind spot
is right behind them.

410
00:48:30,940 --> 00:48:34,610
I've located an ion trail
which leads off-world.

411
00:48:34,777 --> 00:48:37,155
Then you should be off-world, Vaako.

412
00:48:37,238 --> 00:48:39,866
I've deployed a tracker team.
One of the best.

413
00:48:39,949 --> 00:48:41,868
Wherever Riddick has gone,

414
00:48:41,951 --> 00:48:45,330
you lens him out
and cleanse him. You.

415
00:48:45,538 --> 00:48:48,624
You want me to take a frigate
for one breeder?

416
00:48:48,708 --> 00:48:50,752
Don't question it, Vaako!

417
00:48:53,296 --> 00:48:55,965
Take it on faith.

418
00:48:59,427 --> 00:49:02,305
He's always
been unsettled around you.

419
00:49:02,680 --> 00:49:06,601
The Lord Marshal. Unsteady.

420
00:49:07,769 --> 00:49:11,189
Perhaps because he knows
he's half the warrior you are.

421
00:49:11,856 --> 00:49:14,525
Some say he's too artistic
for the job.

422
00:49:16,152 --> 00:49:19,614
I wouldn't be surprised
if someone promoted him soon

423
00:49:19,947 --> 00:49:21,407
to full dead.

424
00:49:24,535 --> 00:49:28,331
- Take care what you say.
- Should I say it softly?

425
00:49:29,207 --> 00:49:31,667
So it sounds more like conspiracy?

426
00:49:32,168 --> 00:49:34,879
Why is it that when anyone breathes
about the demise

427
00:49:34,962 --> 00:49:38,091
of him on the throne
everyone assumes a conspiracy?

428
00:49:40,510 --> 00:49:43,846
Why isn't that
just prudent planning?

429
00:49:44,055 --> 00:49:46,599
When he is ready,
he will name a successor.

430
00:49:46,682 --> 00:49:47,725
Who?

431
00:49:48,559 --> 00:49:50,770
Toal? Scales?

432
00:49:51,646 --> 00:49:53,106
The Purifier?

433
00:49:53,481 --> 00:49:55,108
None of them

434
00:49:55,274 --> 00:49:58,236
with the strength, the dignity

435
00:49:58,653 --> 00:50:00,196
of Lord Vaako.

436
00:50:02,281 --> 00:50:04,367
You can keep what you kill.

437
00:50:04,617 --> 00:50:05,743
Stop.

438
00:50:05,827 --> 00:50:07,954
That is the Necromonger way.

439
00:50:08,496 --> 00:50:10,748
I said stop.

440
00:50:11,499 --> 00:50:14,919
His death will come in due time
and not a moment sooner.

441
00:50:15,002 --> 00:50:16,045
Why?

442
00:50:16,170 --> 00:50:18,089
Because I serve him.
We all serve him.

443
00:50:18,172 --> 00:50:20,800
- It's called fidelity.
- It's called stupidity.

444
00:50:30,726 --> 00:50:32,687
Well, finally, some attention.

445
00:50:46,451 --> 00:50:48,661
You have such greatness in you.

446
00:50:48,744 --> 00:50:50,997
If only you could see it like I do.

447
00:50:54,041 --> 00:50:55,710
You know what I want?

448
00:50:57,253 --> 00:51:00,923
Today I came up behind him
in perfect silence and he knew.

449
00:51:02,508 --> 00:51:05,011
I want to go down to Necropolis.

450
00:51:06,220 --> 00:51:07,430
Right now.

451
00:51:08,514 --> 00:51:11,267
His half-dead soul
sensed I was behind him.

452
00:51:11,350 --> 00:51:12,977
He sees everything.

453
00:51:13,060 --> 00:51:16,606
When no one is looking,
when no one's around,

454
00:51:18,024 --> 00:51:20,234
I'm gonna get down on my knees

455
00:51:22,987 --> 00:51:25,239
while you sit on the throne.

456
00:51:48,179 --> 00:51:49,222
How unexpected...

457
00:51:49,305 --> 00:51:52,183
An Elemental. Here?

458
00:51:52,308 --> 00:51:54,101
One of the captives.

459
00:51:56,103 --> 00:52:00,525
And why, after 30 years,
should it be you?

460
00:52:00,608 --> 00:52:03,402
He doesn't regard her
as a captive, though.

461
00:52:03,486 --> 00:52:07,740
Elementals. They talk of neutrality,
but they're all witches and spies.

462
00:52:07,823 --> 00:52:10,785
Why else would they come
and go like the wind?

463
00:52:11,202 --> 00:52:15,122
But where has he gone?
Where is the Furyan hiding now?

464
00:52:16,666 --> 00:52:19,460
You be the good warrior.
Go after this Riddick.

465
00:52:21,045 --> 00:52:24,799
I'll find out why the Lord Marshal
is so threatened by him.

466
00:53:25,860 --> 00:53:28,362
Do you know
you grind your teeth at night?

467
00:53:30,781 --> 00:53:32,116
Sexy.

468
00:53:47,798 --> 00:53:51,594
Destination reached.
Unlocking manual controls.

469
00:53:51,719 --> 00:53:54,430
All right, I make 700 degrees
on the day side.

470
00:53:55,723 --> 00:53:57,725
300 below on the night side.

471
00:53:57,808 --> 00:53:59,894
Let's not get caught in the sun.

472
00:54:00,603 --> 00:54:05,024
If I owned this place and hell,
I'd rent this place out

473
00:54:05,107 --> 00:54:06,317
and live in hell.

474
00:54:14,909 --> 00:54:17,620
- Slue angle: Good.
- Stand by.

475
00:54:18,829 --> 00:54:22,249
- And...
- Plotted course,

476
00:54:22,750 --> 00:54:24,335
- good.
- Hit it!

477
00:54:25,920 --> 00:54:28,839
Angle of approach: Not good.

478
00:54:36,639 --> 00:54:38,933
Look, Ma, no hands!

479
00:55:13,968 --> 00:55:15,469
Party poppers!

480
00:55:38,117 --> 00:55:39,952
I think I shit myself.

481
00:55:41,412 --> 00:55:44,665
Skittish, Toombs. Very skittish.

482
00:56:06,854 --> 00:56:08,063
Comfy?

483
00:56:26,415 --> 00:56:31,337
When the ride's over,
your goggles are mine.

484
00:57:00,282 --> 00:57:02,117
Four-way split!

485
00:57:13,754 --> 00:57:16,090
29.4 kilometers.

486
00:57:25,015 --> 00:57:27,977
So this is Riddick.

487
00:57:54,253 --> 00:57:58,215
What in the bowels of Christ
are you talking about? 700,000?

488
00:57:58,299 --> 00:57:59,633
Don't take this one, boss.

489
00:57:59,717 --> 00:58:02,970
See, Anatoli here
has a nose for trouble.

490
00:58:03,137 --> 00:58:06,807
- And this one, this Riddick guy...
- Big, big trouble.

491
00:58:06,891 --> 00:58:10,394
So 700,000 is good money.

492
00:58:11,437 --> 00:58:13,564
I'd take the money, Toombs.

493
00:58:23,657 --> 00:58:27,244
The guild pays us a caretaker's fee
for each prisoner each year.

494
00:58:27,328 --> 00:58:31,040
We pay mercs 20% of that total fee
based on a certain life expectancy.

495
00:58:31,373 --> 00:58:32,958
How's about this?

496
00:58:33,208 --> 00:58:36,462
You open that safe you got hidden
behind the console there,

497
00:58:36,545 --> 00:58:39,590
show me the real books.
Then we figure out my cut.

498
00:58:39,673 --> 00:58:41,342
Then I'll be on my way.

499
00:58:46,931 --> 00:58:50,267
Open my books.
This is what you suggest?

500
00:58:55,189 --> 00:58:56,690
Wasn't a suggestion.

501
00:59:15,292 --> 00:59:19,380
These are dangerous days,
if you believe the talk.

502
00:59:20,673 --> 00:59:23,884
- Talk?
- About dead planets.

503
00:59:24,176 --> 00:59:27,054
About some ghost army.

504
00:59:27,721 --> 00:59:29,890
About them.

505
00:59:30,391 --> 00:59:31,642
Them?

506
00:59:49,576 --> 00:59:53,497
I'll run the numbers again.
It takes a couple of days probably.

507
00:59:54,415 --> 00:59:57,209
So you can stay as my guest.

508
00:59:58,002 --> 01:00:01,213
At least here we are all safe. Yes?

509
01:00:01,463 --> 01:00:02,840
Yes, boss.

510
01:00:03,632 --> 01:00:05,342
I'll give it a day.

511
01:00:08,178 --> 01:00:09,263
One.

512
01:00:47,968 --> 01:00:51,889
There are inmates,
and there are convicts.

513
01:00:53,098 --> 01:00:56,101
A convict has a certain code.

514
01:00:56,810 --> 01:01:00,689
And he knows to show
a certain respect.

515
01:01:01,648 --> 01:01:04,318
An inmate, on the other hand,

516
01:01:04,401 --> 01:01:07,112
pulls the pin on his fellow man.

517
01:01:07,196 --> 01:01:11,033
Does the guards' work for them.
Brings shame

518
01:01:12,451 --> 01:01:14,078
to the game.

519
01:01:15,746 --> 01:01:17,790
So which are you gonna be?

520
01:01:19,333 --> 01:01:20,375
Me?

521
01:01:23,962 --> 01:01:26,006
I'm just passing through.

522
01:01:32,221 --> 01:01:34,098
Welcome to Crematoria.

523
01:01:40,312 --> 01:01:42,314
Should I go for the sweet spot?

524
01:01:42,815 --> 01:01:44,566
Left of the spine,
fourth lumbar down,

525
01:01:44,650 --> 01:01:46,151
the abdominal aorta.

526
01:01:46,443 --> 01:01:47,778
What a gusher.

527
01:01:51,323 --> 01:01:54,868
- How do I get eyes like that?
- You got to kill a few people.

528
01:01:56,703 --> 01:01:59,123
Did that. Did a lot of that.

529
01:02:01,708 --> 01:02:03,710
And then you got to
get sent to a slam.

530
01:02:03,794 --> 01:02:05,921
One where you're told
you won't see daylight again?

531
01:02:06,004 --> 01:02:08,173
There wasn't a doctor
who could shine my eyes,

532
01:02:08,257 --> 01:02:11,760
not even for 20 menthol Kools.
Was anything you said true?

533
01:02:13,846 --> 01:02:17,349
What are you gonna do?
Go for the sweet spot?

534
01:02:17,432 --> 01:02:20,686
Remember who
you're talking to, Jack.

535
01:02:22,229 --> 01:02:23,647
Jack's dead.

536
01:02:24,356 --> 01:02:25,816
She was weak.

537
01:02:27,776 --> 01:02:29,278
She couldn't cut it.

538
01:02:42,541 --> 01:02:44,334
The name's Kyra now.

539
01:02:45,085 --> 01:02:46,920
And I'm a new animal.

540
01:03:24,082 --> 01:03:25,792
They can be quite a test.

541
01:03:26,376 --> 01:03:28,086
These deep runs.

542
01:03:29,630 --> 01:03:31,465
Test of our inner selves.

543
01:03:33,842 --> 01:03:35,594
Don't you find that true?

544
01:03:40,515 --> 01:03:42,059
Some men do.

545
01:03:44,269 --> 01:03:46,355
Just being so far from the armada,

546
01:03:46,438 --> 01:03:50,776
the mind can start to fill
with strange thoughts.

547
01:03:51,026 --> 01:03:52,069
Doubts.

548
01:03:52,903 --> 01:03:55,030
Don't you ever have doubts, Vaako?

549
01:03:58,909 --> 01:04:01,161
- Doubts?
- About the campaign.

550
01:04:02,204 --> 01:04:03,664
About Lord Marshal.

551
01:04:06,291 --> 01:04:10,420
First and always,
I am a Necromonger commander.

552
01:04:11,755 --> 01:04:13,966
So if you're here
to test my loyalty,

553
01:04:14,049 --> 01:04:16,593
you succeed
only in testing my patience.

554
01:04:16,843 --> 01:04:20,055
No, that's not why I'm here at all.

555
01:04:42,119 --> 01:04:45,080
I'm so glad I could steal you
away for a moment.

556
01:04:45,163 --> 01:04:47,207
Doesn't it strike you odd?

557
01:04:47,749 --> 01:04:50,502
Here we have
the current Lord Marshal,

558
01:04:50,585 --> 01:04:52,963
destroying entire societies,

559
01:04:53,046 --> 01:04:57,634
and yet he can't bring himself
to kill one stranded Elemental.

560
01:04:58,343 --> 01:04:59,761
Why is that?

561
01:05:01,263 --> 01:05:05,183
You don't pray to our God.
You pray to no God, I hear.

562
01:05:05,892 --> 01:05:09,062
Elementals, we calculate.

563
01:05:10,480 --> 01:05:11,982
Don't we all.

564
01:05:13,191 --> 01:05:15,986
But now let's have
first things first.

565
01:05:16,069 --> 01:05:17,571
What of Riddick?

566
01:05:17,946 --> 01:05:19,656
In truth, I don't know
where he went.

567
01:05:19,740 --> 01:05:22,701
In truth, I'm more interested in
where he came from.

568
01:05:25,787 --> 01:05:27,664
Watch your step.

569
01:05:27,748 --> 01:05:30,876
I've always wondered,
does an air Elemental fly?

570
01:05:32,336 --> 01:05:34,046
Now do me a favor.

571
01:05:34,171 --> 01:05:37,716
Calculate the odds of you
getting off this planet alive

572
01:05:39,092 --> 01:05:41,094
and now cut them in half.

573
01:05:42,429 --> 01:05:46,266
No, we can't fly.
But we glide very well.

574
01:05:46,975 --> 01:05:49,269
Save your threats, Necromonger.

575
01:05:49,895 --> 01:05:53,106
I would have told you about Riddick
for the asking.

576
01:05:53,690 --> 01:05:55,359
It concerns a foretelling,

577
01:05:55,442 --> 01:05:58,070
a prediction
now more than 30 years old.

578
01:05:58,153 --> 01:06:01,365
A young warrior once consulted
a seer.

579
01:06:01,865 --> 01:06:06,244
He was told a child would be born
on the planet Furya, a male child

580
01:06:06,953 --> 01:06:10,624
who would someday
cause the Warrior's downfall.

581
01:06:11,625 --> 01:06:14,294
Cause his untimed death.

582
01:06:16,088 --> 01:06:19,383
Furya? Furya's a ruined world.

583
01:06:19,466 --> 01:06:21,259
No life to speak of.

584
01:06:21,385 --> 01:06:22,928
For good reason.

585
01:06:23,095 --> 01:06:27,349
This young warrior
mounted an attack on Furya

586
01:06:27,808 --> 01:06:30,102
killing all young males
he could find,

587
01:06:30,185 --> 01:06:34,189
even strangling some
with their birth cords.

588
01:06:35,774 --> 01:06:38,110
An artful stroke,
wouldn't you say?

589
01:06:39,820 --> 01:06:42,906
So this warrior, the one who
tried to outwit the prediction,

590
01:06:42,989 --> 01:06:44,408
would later become...

591
01:06:44,491 --> 01:06:46,326
That's why he worries.

592
01:06:46,410 --> 01:06:47,911
...our Lord Marshal.

593
01:06:49,621 --> 01:06:51,665
Which would make the man-child...

594
01:06:51,748 --> 01:06:54,668
He worries he missed
killing that child in its crib.

595
01:06:55,585 --> 01:06:56,711
...Riddick!

596
01:07:13,353 --> 01:07:14,938
That's why it's so vital to him.

597
01:07:15,021 --> 01:07:16,022
Wait.

598
01:07:16,106 --> 01:07:18,275
- It's about a prophecy.
- Wait! Wait!

599
01:07:20,986 --> 01:07:22,487
Are you there?

600
01:07:26,616 --> 01:07:28,702
You do what your lord asks.

601
01:07:28,994 --> 01:07:31,955
You cleanse Riddick for him,
and in doing so,

602
01:07:32,622 --> 01:07:35,417
you prove your undying loyalty.

603
01:07:36,042 --> 01:07:37,961
And perhaps then

604
01:07:38,587 --> 01:07:41,506
he'll finally let down his guard.

605
01:08:24,883 --> 01:08:26,384
Still here, I see.

606
01:08:26,927 --> 01:08:29,846
I've been here 18 years. See this?

607
01:08:32,015 --> 01:08:33,850
I remember how gorgeous she was.

608
01:08:33,934 --> 01:08:37,020
Well, gorgeous in a certain light.

609
01:08:37,854 --> 01:08:40,732
And now,
for the goddamn death of me,

610
01:08:40,815 --> 01:08:42,734
I cannot remember her name.

611
01:08:42,859 --> 01:08:44,653
Feeding time!

612
01:08:50,700 --> 01:08:53,620
We're here for the rest of
our unnatural lives.

613
01:09:02,128 --> 01:09:03,964
Here they come!

614
01:09:09,594 --> 01:09:12,639
Whatever you do,
don't make eye contact.

615
01:09:32,492 --> 01:09:33,994
To the cages!

616
01:10:02,147 --> 01:10:03,440
Let me in!

617
01:11:38,868 --> 01:11:40,662
It's an animal thing.

618
01:11:51,631 --> 01:11:55,385
Check her for me.
She's always got a blade somewhere.

619
01:12:54,903 --> 01:12:57,530
I don't think
she likes being touched.

620
01:13:00,033 --> 01:13:03,870
I'd take my wounded and go
while you still can.

621
01:13:09,959 --> 01:13:13,463
Is there a name for
this private little world of yours?

622
01:13:14,881 --> 01:13:18,426
What happens there
when we don't just run away?

623
01:13:19,052 --> 01:13:21,346
You'll kill us with a soup cup?

624
01:13:23,097 --> 01:13:24,599
Tea, actually.

625
01:13:24,891 --> 01:13:26,267
What's that?

626
01:13:28,520 --> 01:13:30,730
I'll kill you with my tea cup.

627
01:13:43,660 --> 01:13:45,119
You know the rule.

628
01:13:45,203 --> 01:13:48,248
They aren't dead
if they're still on the books.

629
01:14:08,059 --> 01:14:09,269
Come on.

630
01:14:32,125 --> 01:14:33,751
Death by tea cup.

631
01:14:38,506 --> 01:14:41,175
Damn. Why didn't I think of that?

632
01:14:41,301 --> 01:14:43,887
I didn't come here
to play "Who's The Better Killer?"

633
01:14:43,970 --> 01:14:46,973
But it's my favorite game.
Haven't you heard?

634
01:14:47,181 --> 01:14:48,975
I heard you came looking for me.

635
01:14:49,058 --> 01:14:51,895
Is that all?
Then you missed the good part.

636
01:14:52,520 --> 01:14:54,772
Hooked up with some mercs
out of Lupus Five.

637
01:14:54,856 --> 01:14:58,693
Said they'd take me on, teach me
the trade, give me a good cut.

638
01:14:59,736 --> 01:15:01,404
They slaved me out, Riddick.

639
01:15:01,487 --> 01:15:04,240
Do you know what that could do
to you when you're that age?

640
01:15:04,324 --> 01:15:07,994
- When you're 12 years old?
- I told you to stay in New Mecca.

641
01:15:08,328 --> 01:15:10,079
Did you not listen?

642
01:15:10,872 --> 01:15:14,542
I had mercs on my neck.
I'll always have mercs on my neck.

643
01:15:15,418 --> 01:15:19,589
I spent five years on a frozen heap
just to keep them away from you.

644
01:15:20,131 --> 01:15:22,800
And you go and sign up
with the same fake badges

645
01:15:22,884 --> 01:15:25,136
that wanted to cut you up
and use you for bait.

646
01:15:25,219 --> 01:15:27,513
What are you pitching, Riddick?

647
01:15:28,097 --> 01:15:29,766
That you cutting out
was a good thing?

648
01:15:29,849 --> 01:15:33,144
That you had my ass covered
from halfway across the universe?

649
01:15:33,227 --> 01:15:35,063
You signed with mercs.

650
01:15:39,525 --> 01:15:41,778
There was nobody else around.

651
01:15:56,459 --> 01:15:59,462
Let's pop the cork.
Get some fresh air.

652
01:16:36,416 --> 01:16:38,584
So they do go topside

653
01:16:39,919 --> 01:16:41,546
to swap out air.

654
01:16:42,797 --> 01:16:44,215
Interesting.

655
01:16:45,341 --> 01:16:47,176
Who the hell are you?

656
01:16:49,387 --> 01:16:51,889
When it happens, it'll happen fast.

657
01:16:51,973 --> 01:16:55,393
Stay on my leg when I cut fence,
or stay here.

658
01:16:55,977 --> 01:16:58,104
For the rest of your unnatural life.

659
01:16:58,938 --> 01:17:01,607
Nobody outs this place. Nobody.

660
01:17:07,989 --> 01:17:09,657
He ain't nobody.

661
01:17:24,297 --> 01:17:25,882
Good news first.

662
01:17:25,965 --> 01:17:28,634
Talked things over
with my amigos here.

663
01:17:28,718 --> 01:17:31,763
We'll cut you in for 775,000.

664
01:17:34,640 --> 01:17:37,477
All right. What's the bad news?

665
01:17:37,560 --> 01:17:39,937
They close the local whorehouse?

666
01:17:41,647 --> 01:17:45,151
No. The bad news is worse than that.
Much worse.

667
01:17:45,735 --> 01:17:48,279
Our pilot, he saw this.

668
01:17:49,155 --> 01:17:51,282
It crossed a shipping lane.

669
01:17:53,868 --> 01:17:56,829
Any idea what this might be?

670
01:18:01,209 --> 01:18:03,252
Never saw nothing like it.

671
01:18:04,462 --> 01:18:07,131
This ship charts back
to Helion Prime.

672
01:18:08,841 --> 01:18:11,761
You know, Anatoli's got
a nose for trouble

673
01:18:11,844 --> 01:18:15,515
and he thinks
trouble follows you here.

674
01:18:18,684 --> 01:18:22,105
Look, we dusted our tracks
and got the hell out of there.

675
01:18:22,188 --> 01:18:24,690
There is no way we didn't lose them.

676
01:18:26,859 --> 01:18:28,027
Them?

677
01:18:35,284 --> 01:18:37,036
This is my prisoner.

678
01:18:37,370 --> 01:18:39,705
Mine. Nobody else's.

679
01:18:39,872 --> 01:18:42,166
And I want my money now.

680
01:18:45,002 --> 01:18:48,673
You stole a prisoner from them?

681
01:19:58,701 --> 01:20:00,786
Riddick, no!

682
01:20:08,794 --> 01:20:11,255
Should've taken the money, Toombs.

683
01:21:06,644 --> 01:21:08,437
Are you going to kill me?

684
01:21:44,181 --> 01:21:45,391
Mercs.

685
01:21:46,142 --> 01:21:49,270
Some guards here,
but this can't be all of them.

686
01:21:50,146 --> 01:21:53,316
Check their slots in the back.
And be careful.

687
01:21:53,816 --> 01:21:56,569
Don't bother. Guards ain't there.

688
01:21:58,154 --> 01:22:00,865
They figured out
the Necros are coming for me.

689
01:22:00,948 --> 01:22:03,409
Plan was to clean the bank,
ghost the mercs,

690
01:22:03,492 --> 01:22:05,411
break wide through the tunnel.

691
01:22:05,494 --> 01:22:09,665
Then somebody got a lucky shot off
with this rocket launcher here

692
01:22:09,749 --> 01:22:11,667
and took out the sled.

693
01:22:12,001 --> 01:22:14,003
Guards took off on foot

694
01:22:14,086 --> 01:22:16,672
but rigged the door
so no one could follow.

695
01:22:16,756 --> 01:22:19,550
They'll take the one ship
in the hangar

696
01:22:20,176 --> 01:22:22,720
and leave everyone else here to die.

697
01:22:22,928 --> 01:22:25,306
How come you know all this shit?

698
01:22:25,598 --> 01:22:27,433
You weren't even here.

699
01:22:28,434 --> 01:22:30,311
'Cause it was my plan.

700
01:22:35,858 --> 01:22:38,110
I should have taken the money.

701
01:22:45,826 --> 01:22:47,453
Riddick!

702
01:22:57,922 --> 01:23:00,758
What is this?
What is he thinking?

703
01:23:01,092 --> 01:23:04,053
- Once that sun comes up...
- We'll last five minutes.

704
01:23:04,470 --> 01:23:08,391
Five minutes. We ain't gonna last
30 seconds out there.

705
01:23:08,474 --> 01:23:10,476
It'll light you up like a match.

706
01:23:15,314 --> 01:23:18,943
20-mile buffer zone
and 30 klicks to the hangar.

707
01:23:21,737 --> 01:23:24,073
30 klicks, over that terrain?

708
01:23:37,294 --> 01:23:41,173
It's moving in the right direction.
We could make it.

709
01:23:42,508 --> 01:23:44,510
Stay behind the night,

710
01:23:45,010 --> 01:23:46,679
ahead of the sun.

711
01:23:47,263 --> 01:23:49,390
There's gonna be one speed.

712
01:23:52,393 --> 01:23:53,561
Mine.

713
01:23:55,396 --> 01:23:58,816
If you can't keep up, don't step up.
You'll just die.

714
01:25:19,772 --> 01:25:21,440
Go! Come on, go!

715
01:25:22,107 --> 01:25:23,442
Climb here!

716
01:25:23,776 --> 01:25:25,945
Climb! Go!

717
01:25:52,429 --> 01:25:53,472
Boss!

718
01:25:57,184 --> 01:25:58,227
Up there.

719
01:25:59,186 --> 01:26:01,855
- Take a look.
- Because Anatoli says so?

720
01:26:02,523 --> 01:26:04,650
Because his nose says so.

721
01:26:21,792 --> 01:26:23,502
There's nothing up here.

722
01:26:38,183 --> 01:26:39,476
Riddick.

723
01:26:41,186 --> 01:26:43,105
They're heading
for the volcano fields.

724
01:26:43,188 --> 01:26:44,273
Going for our ship!

725
01:26:44,356 --> 01:26:46,817
No chance do they
get to the hangar first. No chance!

726
01:26:57,995 --> 01:27:00,539
Next one! Next hole!
We'll catch them there!

727
01:27:28,901 --> 01:27:30,903
No more running for you.

728
01:27:36,492 --> 01:27:38,535
Where did the big guy go?

729
01:28:12,444 --> 01:28:13,445
Close it!

730
01:28:45,894 --> 01:28:48,397
What was that?
You don't care if you live or die?

731
01:28:48,480 --> 01:28:50,899
If I kill them first, not really.

732
01:28:53,235 --> 01:28:54,611
Maybe I do.

733
01:28:55,487 --> 01:28:56,905
Keep moving!

734
01:29:54,880 --> 01:29:56,048
Kyra?

735
01:29:58,217 --> 01:29:59,676
- Kyra!
- What?

736
01:30:00,177 --> 01:30:02,721
Get that ass moving!

737
01:30:41,718 --> 01:30:42,928
Riddick?

738
01:30:47,766 --> 01:30:51,645
Remember what I said
about not caring if I lived or died?

739
01:30:55,691 --> 01:30:57,943
You knew I was kidding, right?

740
01:31:01,029 --> 01:31:02,406
One speed.

741
01:31:22,926 --> 01:31:24,636
Temperature differential.

742
01:31:25,512 --> 01:31:26,889
Your rope.

743
01:31:27,723 --> 01:31:30,058
It's too late.
We're never gonna make it.

744
01:31:30,142 --> 01:31:32,269
Your rope! Give me your rope!

745
01:31:33,312 --> 01:31:35,397
And your water. All of it!

746
01:31:36,273 --> 01:31:38,483
Stay in the shadow of the mountain.

747
01:31:38,567 --> 01:31:40,485
Don't wait for me. Run!

748
01:31:51,914 --> 01:31:53,165
Riddick!

749
01:32:38,043 --> 01:32:40,253
Where the hell is that hangar?

750
01:32:45,884 --> 01:32:47,344
There it is.

751
01:32:50,889 --> 01:32:52,099
Listen.

752
01:33:21,378 --> 01:33:23,547
Let me guess. Necros.

753
01:33:24,006 --> 01:33:26,758
And a whole lot of Necro firepower.

754
01:33:27,259 --> 01:33:30,137
Shit! I hate not being the bad guys.

755
01:33:58,665 --> 01:34:00,542
I figure we got three minutes

756
01:34:00,625 --> 01:34:03,545
before the sun hits us again,
burns out this whole valley.

757
01:34:03,628 --> 01:34:04,755
Wait.

758
01:34:04,963 --> 01:34:07,007
We gonna do this or not?

759
01:34:07,340 --> 01:34:08,717
Just wait.

760
01:34:13,680 --> 01:34:14,931
Ellen.

761
01:34:16,558 --> 01:34:19,186
Her name was Ellen.
I never really forgot.

762
01:34:38,955 --> 01:34:40,123
Boss!

763
01:34:51,259 --> 01:34:53,428
Remember that
favorite game of yours?

764
01:34:53,512 --> 01:34:55,514
"Who's The Better Killer?"

765
01:34:57,349 --> 01:34:58,683
Let's play.

766
01:35:00,352 --> 01:35:01,686
Come on!

767
01:35:19,412 --> 01:35:21,164
On the right!

768
01:35:29,089 --> 01:35:30,841
- Watch out!
- Behind you!

769
01:36:28,732 --> 01:36:30,066
Sybar!

770
01:36:49,794 --> 01:36:50,837
No!

771
01:38:16,131 --> 01:38:17,799
Get up. Get up.

772
01:38:18,717 --> 01:38:20,385
Please get up.

773
01:38:34,232 --> 01:38:38,486
So, you can kneel.

774
01:38:57,213 --> 01:38:58,882
I think you know now.

775
01:39:01,343 --> 01:39:04,095
I think you know
who tore Furya apart.

776
01:39:07,098 --> 01:39:10,727
This mark carries the anger
of an entire race.

777
01:39:16,399 --> 01:39:18,026
But it's going to hurt.

778
01:41:36,706 --> 01:41:37,832
Kyra?

779
01:41:42,212 --> 01:41:44,756
I was supposed to
deliver a message to you

780
01:41:47,091 --> 01:41:49,219
if Vaako failed to kill you.

781
01:41:51,262 --> 01:41:54,015
A message from
the Lord Marshal himself.

782
01:41:55,934 --> 01:41:58,269
He tells you
to stay away from Helion.

783
01:41:58,353 --> 01:42:00,104
Stay away from him.

784
01:42:00,897 --> 01:42:03,650
And in return,
you'll be hunted no more.

785
01:42:10,114 --> 01:42:13,117
But Vaako will most likely
report you as dead.

786
01:42:14,202 --> 01:42:16,287
So this is your chance.

787
01:42:17,455 --> 01:42:20,458
Your chance to do
what no man has ever done.

788
01:42:21,584 --> 01:42:22,877
The girl.

789
01:42:23,211 --> 01:42:25,129
Where will they take her?

790
01:42:42,313 --> 01:42:45,567
We all began as something else.

791
01:42:49,904 --> 01:42:54,242
I've done unbelievable things

792
01:42:55,285 --> 01:42:58,246
in the name of a faith
that was never my own.

793
01:43:00,164 --> 01:43:03,376
And he'll do to her
what he did to me.

794
01:43:10,425 --> 01:43:14,262
The Necromonger in me
warns you not to go back.

795
01:43:16,472 --> 01:43:18,349
But the Furyan in me

796
01:43:22,687 --> 01:43:24,647
hopes you won't listen.

797
01:43:30,528 --> 01:43:34,032
God knows I've dreamed of it.

798
01:44:37,136 --> 01:44:39,514
I have lost a Purifier

799
01:44:40,306 --> 01:44:44,310
but I have gained
a First among commanders.

800
01:44:45,978 --> 01:44:47,980
It is overdue, isn't it,

801
01:44:48,898 --> 01:44:51,901
that we acknowledge
your many accomplishments,

802
01:44:52,485 --> 01:44:54,320
your steady faith

803
01:44:54,654 --> 01:44:56,280
and above all,

804
01:44:56,739 --> 01:44:59,075
your unflinching loyalty?

805
01:45:07,166 --> 01:45:10,795
Obedience without question.
Loyalty till UnderVerse come.

806
01:45:13,131 --> 01:45:14,799
Well done, Vaako.

807
01:45:16,926 --> 01:45:19,971
This is a day of days.

808
01:45:39,657 --> 01:45:41,784
Look more pleased, Vaako.

809
01:45:43,828 --> 01:45:46,789
You have killed his enemy

810
01:45:47,498 --> 01:45:49,000
and his suspicions.

811
01:45:49,167 --> 01:45:50,877
I should have brought back his head.

812
01:45:50,960 --> 01:45:54,088
You saw him unbreathing.
You saw him dead on the ground.

813
01:45:54,172 --> 01:45:55,757
Riddick was no common breeder.

814
01:45:55,840 --> 01:45:57,508
In a heartbeat
he dropped 20 of my men.

815
01:45:57,592 --> 01:46:00,845
All mysteries are not miracles,
not even in this religion.

816
01:46:03,639 --> 01:46:06,517
And if you say it is certain,
then it is certain.

817
01:46:07,185 --> 01:46:09,729
And we've already said it,
haven't we?

818
01:46:12,064 --> 01:46:13,524
We have.

819
01:46:18,279 --> 01:46:20,364
Now, tell me if it's true.

820
01:46:20,531 --> 01:46:22,325
Tell me the Furyan is gone

821
01:46:22,408 --> 01:46:26,162
and I can close this campaign
without hearing his boot steps.

822
01:46:26,579 --> 01:46:28,206
If he is dead.

823
01:46:29,540 --> 01:46:32,335
I sense I'm not far
from the same fate,

824
01:46:32,877 --> 01:46:35,171
being of no further use here.

825
01:46:35,546 --> 01:46:38,633
Shouldn't I tell you
that Riddick is still alive?

826
01:46:38,716 --> 01:46:40,468
Don't try me, Aereon.

827
01:46:40,551 --> 01:46:43,221
I could plow you under
with the rest of Helion Prime.

828
01:46:43,304 --> 01:46:44,972
No one really knows the future.

829
01:46:45,056 --> 01:46:46,891
Then tell me the odds.

830
01:46:47,058 --> 01:46:49,227
That Vaako met with success.

831
01:46:49,560 --> 01:46:52,146
That I will now be the one
who can carry his people

832
01:46:52,230 --> 01:46:54,440
across the threshold
into UnderVerse,

833
01:46:54,524 --> 01:46:56,317
where they shall begin true life.

834
01:46:56,400 --> 01:46:58,611
Tell me what I want to hear, Aereon.

835
01:46:59,028 --> 01:47:01,614
And maybe
I'll save your home world

836
01:47:02,240 --> 01:47:03,574
for last.

837
01:47:07,954 --> 01:47:09,330
The odds are good.

838
01:47:09,413 --> 01:47:10,456
That?

839
01:47:10,790 --> 01:47:13,376
That you will reach
the UnderVerse

840
01:47:15,962 --> 01:47:17,046
soon.

841
01:47:56,711 --> 01:47:58,296
Ascension protocol!

842
01:47:58,421 --> 01:48:00,673
We still have numbers out there,
Lord Marshal.

843
01:48:00,756 --> 01:48:02,341
Sweep teams, recon ships.

844
01:48:02,425 --> 01:48:05,219
They would be hard-pressed
to make it back...

845
01:48:09,098 --> 01:48:12,143
Get my armada off the ground.

846
01:49:14,872 --> 01:49:18,125
- You mean on Helion?
- I mean here on this very ship.

847
01:49:18,209 --> 01:49:20,002
Could you be wrong?

848
01:49:20,544 --> 01:49:23,506
Mind fabricates fear.
Could you be wrong?

849
01:49:23,589 --> 01:49:26,509
Not so wrong as you
when you left him alive!

850
01:49:26,717 --> 01:49:28,511
It's twice a mistake.

851
01:49:28,594 --> 01:49:32,014
Not only your failure,
but now the report of success.

852
01:49:32,181 --> 01:49:34,684
How do we salvage this? How?

853
01:49:35,893 --> 01:49:38,229
Lord Marshal's got to be warned.

854
01:49:38,729 --> 01:49:41,190
You will never see the UnderVerse!

855
01:49:41,691 --> 01:49:44,443
He will kill us both
before our due time.

856
01:49:47,071 --> 01:49:49,240
I say give Riddick his chance.

857
01:49:53,661 --> 01:49:56,080
If he is half of what you think,

858
01:49:56,330 --> 01:49:58,457
he can at least wound
the Lord Marshal.

859
01:49:58,541 --> 01:50:01,002
And that is when you must act.

860
01:50:01,085 --> 01:50:03,504
Just to take his place?
Just to keep what I kill?

861
01:50:03,587 --> 01:50:05,172
That is the Necromonger way.

862
01:50:05,256 --> 01:50:08,426
- It is not enough!
- Then you do it for the faith!

863
01:50:08,759 --> 01:50:11,595
If he has fear, he has weakness.

864
01:50:12,013 --> 01:50:14,223
If he has weakness, Vaako...

865
01:50:15,599 --> 01:50:17,768
He is unworthy of Lordship.

866
01:50:18,936 --> 01:50:21,230
We do it for all Necromongers.

867
01:50:23,065 --> 01:50:24,775
Protect the faith.

868
01:50:25,109 --> 01:50:27,486
This can still be a day of days.

869
01:50:28,279 --> 01:50:31,032
But the timing must

870
01:50:31,991 --> 01:50:33,409
be flawless.

871
01:50:55,181 --> 01:50:58,434
Final protocol. Execute on my order.

872
01:51:34,178 --> 01:51:35,513
Go inside.

873
01:51:37,765 --> 01:51:39,183
Are they leaving now?

874
01:51:39,266 --> 01:51:41,560
Ziza, go inside.

875
01:52:33,946 --> 01:52:36,031
We found this Lensor dead.

876
01:52:38,659 --> 01:52:40,578
Show me his last sight.

877
01:52:54,133 --> 01:52:55,718
Commander Toal.

878
01:52:56,010 --> 01:52:57,845
He won't escape twice.

879
01:54:52,459 --> 01:54:54,211
Stay your weapons.

880
01:54:55,087 --> 01:54:56,714
He came for me.

881
01:55:23,699 --> 01:55:25,242
Consider this.

882
01:55:31,623 --> 01:55:34,543
If you fall here now,

883
01:55:35,169 --> 01:55:36,879
you'll never rise.

884
01:55:38,047 --> 01:55:40,424
But if you choose another way,

885
01:55:41,300 --> 01:55:43,177
the Necromonger way,

886
01:55:44,094 --> 01:55:46,680
you'll die in due time

887
01:55:46,805 --> 01:55:49,433
and rise again in the UnderVerse.

888
01:55:59,693 --> 01:56:00,944
Go to him.

889
01:56:10,079 --> 01:56:11,497
It hurts

890
01:56:12,289 --> 01:56:13,582
at first.

891
01:56:14,958 --> 01:56:18,712
But after a while, the pain
goes away, just as they promise.

892
01:56:20,756 --> 01:56:22,508
Are you with me, Kyra?

893
01:56:22,591 --> 01:56:26,887
There's a moment when you can almost
see the UnderVerse through his eyes.

894
01:56:27,304 --> 01:56:29,348
He makes it sound perfect.

895
01:56:29,973 --> 01:56:31,850
A place where anyone can start over.

896
01:56:31,934 --> 01:56:34,728
Are you with me, Kyra?

897
01:56:47,116 --> 01:56:48,867
Convert now

898
01:56:49,410 --> 01:56:51,245
or fall forever.

899
01:56:56,500 --> 01:56:58,710
You killed everything I know.

900
01:57:07,886 --> 01:57:09,304
Not yet.

901
01:57:21,024 --> 01:57:24,069
Been a long time
since I've seen my own blood.

902
01:58:42,314 --> 01:58:44,608
These are his last moments.

903
01:59:04,711 --> 01:59:07,005
Give me your soul.

904
01:59:12,302 --> 01:59:13,762
Fuck you!

905
02:00:21,330 --> 02:00:23,874
You are not the one
to bring me down.

906
02:00:42,726 --> 02:00:45,395
Now! Kill the beast
while he's wounded!

907
02:01:02,663 --> 02:01:04,206
Help me, Vaako.

908
02:01:05,082 --> 02:01:06,416
Kill him.

909
02:01:13,965 --> 02:01:15,133
Vaako?

910
02:01:19,930 --> 02:01:21,306
Forgive me.

911
02:01:22,182 --> 02:01:23,475
Flawless.

912
02:01:56,133 --> 02:01:57,175
No.

913
02:02:02,973 --> 02:02:04,099
No!

914
02:02:06,059 --> 02:02:08,520
Now, what would be the odds of that?

915
02:02:22,659 --> 02:02:24,661
I thought you were dead.

916
02:02:27,372 --> 02:02:29,249
Are you with me, Kyra?

917
02:02:32,461 --> 02:02:34,337
I was always with you.

918
02:02:36,840 --> 02:02:38,049
I was.

919
02:04:02,259 --> 02:04:04,177
You keep what you kill.

